      "writtenOn": "2017-10-02T12:48:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As mentioned on my CL from where you\u0027ve ported the code, this was also my original approach but I now think that, as I\u0027ve done in my CL, it\u0027s better to focus each script on one reusable job: Use one script to extracts the package names from a .jar or a set of .java files, plus a separate script to convert a set of package names to a module-info.java.\n\nFor example, because of the problem of overlapping packages (android.util is in both core-libart and framework), we may want to be able to filter out specific package names that should not be exported by a particular runtime image.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "22ee644fd42a23ad6f08b9a07a9386f4833144de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5ffca55c_54ab31e3",
        "filename": "scripts/jars-to-module-info-java.sh",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 4,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-11T19:34:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here\u0027s my thinking:\n\nI don\u0027t like having multiple chained rules if they will always run in sequence and nothing ever needs the intermediates, it just makes dependencies harder, especially if the intermediate rules produce multiple files.\n\nIf everything is a single rule and this script just does the bare minimum it will need a bunch of shell script junk to tie them together, which is harder to maintain in Soong than if it is in a separate shell script.\n\nThe shell script could call other more generic scripts, but that also makes dependencies harder because Soong needs to have a dependency list of what other scripts might be called.",
      "parentUuid": "3ef23e95_1947e48e",
